IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-part16-reverse-onus.l4 -- section 515(4.1) to (4.4) (the conditions a justice must consider or add for listed offences), (6), (6.1) and (7) (the reverse onus) and (10) (the grounds for detention)
-- of the Criminal Code (Canada). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails; a "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING.
-- Offences named by section number are tested against the core's `Provision of the Code` (section as a decimal, subsection as printed). Offences under another Act, and facts the text says are "alleged",
-- are plain inputs. The answers of other parts are inputs named for the section that answers them: `s 469`, `s 3.01`, `s 2 terrorism offence`, `s 2 serious offence` (MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING is carried through).

§ `Helpers -- three-valued conjunction and disjunction over the answers of this subsection`

-- "any answer holds": JUST TRUE if one does; otherwise NOTHING if one is not covered; otherwise JUST FALSE. The text's "any of the following" lists give the answer "no" only when every limb answers "no".
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) answers THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem NOTHING answers THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb of the list rests on an answer of a section outside this range that is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the accused is charged (a) ... (b) ... (b.1) ... (b.2) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (every limb answers no)

-- "all answers hold": JUST FALSE if one is the text's no; otherwise NOTHING if one is not covered; otherwise JUST TRUE.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(6) helper: all answers hold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) answers THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with an indictable offence, other than an offence listed in section 469" (a conjunct answers no)
        IF elem NOTHING answers THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a conjunct rests on an answer of a section outside this range that is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 515(4.1) -- The condition prohibiting possession of firearms and other things`

-- src:11408 | Condition prohibiting possession of firearms, etc.
-- src:11409 | (4.1) When the justice makes an order under subsection (2) in respect of an accused who is charged with any of the following offences, the justice shall add to the order a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all those things, until the accused is dealt with according to law unless the justice considers that such a condition is not required in the interests of the safety of the accused or the safety and security of a victim of the offence or of any other person:
-- src:11410 | (a) an offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted;
-- src:11411 | (b) a terrorism offence;
-- src:11412 | (c) an offence that is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:11413 | (d) [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 48]
-- src:11414 | (e) an offence under section 346 (extortion);
-- src:11415 | (f) an offence under section 423.1 (intimidation of a justice system participant);
-- src:11416 | (g) an offence under subsection 423.2(1) (intimidation — health services);
-- src:11417 | (g.1) an offence under subsection 423.3(1) (intimidation — building used for religious worship, etc.);
-- src:11418 | (h) an offence relating to the contravention of any of sections 9 to 14 of the Cannabis Act;
-- src:11419 | (i) an offence relating to the contravention of any of sections 5 to 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act;
-- src:11420 | (j) an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance;
-- src:11421 | (k) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or an offence under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act that is committed in relation to an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of that Act.
@ref s 515(4.1) (src:11408-11421)
DECLARE `s 515(4.1) the charge` HAS
    `the offence is under the Criminal Code`                                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Code provision the offence is under`                                                                                                     IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted`                                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`                                                                                                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence relates to the contravention of any of sections 9 to 14 of the Cannabis Act`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence relates to the contravention of any of sections 5 to 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is one referred to in paragraph (k): under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act in relation to one of them`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 515(4.1)(a) to (k) (src:11409-11421)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 515(4.1) the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.1) the accused is charged with one of the offences listed in paragraphs (a) to (k)` MEANS
    `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` limbs
    WHERE
        limbs MEANS LIST
            charge's `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted`   -- (a)
            charge's `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`   -- (b)
            JUST (charge's `the offence is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`)   -- (c)
            JUST FALSE   -- (d) [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 48]: no offence is listed  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) [Repealed, 2026, c. 19, s. 48]"
            JUST (`in the Code` AND `section is` 346)   -- (e) section 346 (extortion)
            JUST (`in the Code` AND `section is` 423.1)   -- (f) section 423.1 (intimidation of a justice system participant)
            JUST (`in the Code` AND `section is` 423.2 AND `subsection is` "(1)")   -- (g) subsection 423.2(1)
            JUST (`in the Code` AND `section is` 423.3 AND `subsection is` "(1)")   -- (g.1) subsection 423.3(1)
            JUST (charge's `the offence relates to the contravention of any of sections 9 to 14 of the Cannabis Act`)   -- (h)
            JUST (charge's `the offence relates to the contravention of any of sections 5 to 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`)   -- (i)
            JUST (charge's `the offence involves, or its subject-matter is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance`)   -- (j)
            JUST (charge's `the offence is one referred to in paragraph (k): under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act in relation to one of them`)   -- (k)
        `in the Code` MEANS charge's `the offence is under the Criminal Code`
        `section is` n MEANS charge's `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `section` EQUALS n
        `subsection is` s MEANS charge's `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS s

@ref s 515(4.1) (src:11409)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 515(4.1) listed offences` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the justice considers that such a condition is not required in the interests of the safety of the accused or the safety and security of a victim of the offence or of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.1) the justice must add a condition prohibiting the accused from possessing a firearm and the other things` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is made under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the justice makes an order under subsection (2) in respect of an accused who is charged with any of the following offences, the justice shall add"
        IF `the answer of s 515(4.1) listed offences` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any of the following offences" (a limb rests on an answer of a section outside this range that is not covered)
        IF `the answer of s 515(4.1) listed offences` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of an accused who is charged with any of the following offences"
        IF `the justice considers that such a condition is not required in the interests of the safety of the accused or the safety and security of a victim of the offence or of any other person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the justice considers that such a condition is not required"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11422 | Surrender, etc.
-- src:11423 | (4.11) Where the justice adds a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2), the justice shall specify in the order the manner and method by which
-- src:11424 | (a) the things referred to in subsection (4.1) that are in the possession of the accused shall be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with; and
-- src:11425 | (b) the authorizations, licences and registration certificates held by the person shall be surrendered.
@ref s 515(4.11) (src:11422-11425)
GIVEN `the justice adds a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.11) the justice must specify in the order the manner and method of surrender, disposal, detention or storage` MEANS
    IF `the justice adds a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the justice adds a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2), the justice shall specify in the order the manner and method"

-- src:11426 | Reasons
-- src:11427 | (4.12) Where the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2), the justice shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition.
@ref s 515(4.12) (src:11426-11427)
GIVEN `the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.12) the justice must include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` MEANS
    IF `the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (4.1) to an order made under subsection (2), the justice shall include in the record a statement of the reasons"

§ `Sections 515(4.2) to (4.4) -- Additional conditions to consider`

-- 515(4.3): "The offences for the purposes of subsection (4.2) are (a) a terrorism offence; (a.1) an offence alleged ... for a criminal organization; (b) an offence described in section 346 or 423.1 or subsection 423.2(1) or 423.3(1);
-- (c) an offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, including against the accused's intimate partner; and (d) an offence under [the FISOIA]". "are" is read as closed
-- (fork, as the keel read "are" in s 2.3(1)): an offence that is none of those is the text's no for subsection (4.2).
-- src:11429 | (4.2) Before making an order under subsection (2), in the case of an accused who is charged with an offence referred to in subsection (4.3), the justice shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety and security of any person, particularly a victim of or witness to the offence or a justice system participant, to include as a condition of the order
-- src:11430 | (a) that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:11431 | (a.1) that the accused abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:11432 | (a.2) that the accused wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request; or
-- src:11433 | (b) that the accused comply with any other condition specified in the order that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of those persons.
-- src:11434 | Offences
-- src:11435 | (4.3) The offences for the purposes of subsection (4.2) are
-- src:11436 | (a) a terrorism offence;
-- src:11437 | (a.1) an offence that is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization;
-- src:11438 | (b) an offence described in section 346 or 423.1 or subsection 423.2(1) or 423.3(1);
-- src:11439 | (c) an offence in the commission of which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, including against the accused’s intimate partner; and
-- src:11440 | (d) an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or an offence under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act that is committed in relation to an offence under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of that Act.
@ref s 515(4.2) and (4.3) (src:11429-11440)
DECLARE `s 515(4.3) the charge` HAS
    `the offence is under the Criminal Code`                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Code provision the offence is under`                                                                                         IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`                                                                                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, including against the accused's intimate partner`   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is one referred to in paragraph (d): under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act in relation to one of them`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 515(4.3)(a) to (d) (src:11435-11440)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 515(4.3) the charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.3) the offence is one of the offences for the purposes of subsection (4.2)` MEANS
    `s 515(6) helper: any answer holds` limbs
    WHERE
        limbs MEANS LIST
            charge's `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`   -- (a)
            JUST (charge's `the offence is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`)   -- (a.1)
            JUST (`in the Code` AND (`section is` 346 OR `section is` 423.1 OR (`section is` 423.2 AND `subsection is` "(1)") OR (`section is` 423.3 AND `subsection is` "(1)")))   -- (b)
            charge's `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence against a person was used, threatened or attempted, including against the accused's intimate partner`   -- (c)
            JUST (charge's `the offence is one referred to in paragraph (d): under subsection 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.2(1), 20.3(1) or 20.4(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act, or under subsection 21(1) or 22(1) or section 23 of that Act in relation to one of them`)   -- (d)
        `in the Code` MEANS charge's `the offence is under the Criminal Code`
        `section is` n MEANS charge's `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `section` EQUALS n
        `subsection is` s MEANS charge's `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS s

@ref s 515(4.2)(a) to (b) the conditions (src:11430-11433)
DECLARE `s 515(4.2) the additional condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(4.2)(a) that the accused abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order`
    `s 515(4.2)(a.1) that the accused abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order`
    `s 515(4.2)(a.2) that the accused wear an electronic monitoring device`
    `s 515(4.2)(b) that the accused comply with any other condition specified in the order that the justice considers necessary to ensure the safety and security of those persons`

@ref s 515(4.2) (src:11429-11433)
GIVEN `an order is to be made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 515(4.3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      condition IS A `s 515(4.2) the additional condition`
      `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.2) the justice must consider whether it is desirable to include the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is to be made under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before making an order under subsection (2), in the case of an accused who is charged with an offence referred to in subsection (4.3), the justice shall consider"
        IF `the answer of s 515(4.3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence referred to in subsection (4.3)" (a limb of subsection (4.3) rests on an answer of a section outside this range that is not covered)
        IF `the answer of s 515(4.3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an accused who is charged with an offence referred to in subsection (4.3)"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 515(4.2)(a.2) that the accused wear an electronic monitoring device` AND NOT `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a.2) that the accused wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11441 | Additional conditions
-- src:11442 | (4.4) Before making an order under subsection (2) in respect of an accused who is charged with an offence described in subsection 333.1(1), (3) or (4) or paragraph 348(1)(d), the justice shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the safety and security of any person, particularly a victim of or witness to the offence or a justice system participant, to include as a condition of the order that the accused
-- src:11443 | (a) abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:11444 | (b) abstain from having in their possession any instrument specified in the order that is suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place or motor vehicle; or
-- src:11445 | (c) return to and remain at their place of residence at the times specified in the order.
@ref s 515(4.4) (src:11441-11445)
DECLARE `s 515(4.4) the condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(4.4)(a) that the accused abstain from going to any place or entering any geographic area specified in the order`
    `s 515(4.4)(b) that the accused abstain from having in their possession any instrument specified in the order that is suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place or motor vehicle`
    `s 515(4.4)(c) that the accused return to and remain at their place of residence at the times specified in the order`

@ref s 515(4.4) (src:11441-11445)
GIVEN `an order is to be made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Code provision the offence is under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      condition IS A `s 515(4.4) the condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(4.4) the justice must consider whether it is desirable to include the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an order is to be made under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before making an order under subsection (2) in respect of an accused who is charged with an offence described in subsection 333.1(1), (3) or (4) or paragraph 348(1)(d), the justice shall consider"
        IF NOT (`the offence is under the Criminal Code` AND `the offence is described in subsection 333.1(1), (3) or (4) or paragraph 348(1)(d)`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of an accused who is charged with an offence described in subsection 333.1(1), (3) or (4) or paragraph 348(1)(d)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the offence is described in subsection 333.1(1), (3) or (4) or paragraph 348(1)(d)` MEANS
                (`the Code provision the offence is under`'s `section` EQUALS 333.1 AND (   `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
                                                                                          OR `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"
                                                                                          OR `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(4)"))
            OR (`the Code provision the offence is under`'s `section` EQUALS 348 AND `the Code provision the offence is under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(d)")

§ `Section 515(6) and (7) -- The reverse onus`

-- 515 (6): the accused must show cause why detention is not justified, by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in (10),
-- if the accused is charged (a) with an indictable offence, other than an offence listed in section 469, (i) ... (xiv); (b) with an indictable offence, other than 469, and is not ordinarily resident in Canada; (b.1) ...;
-- (b.2) ...; (c) ...; or (d) .... The limbs are in four functions below: (a), (b), (b.1) and (b.2), (c) and (d), and one that combines them.
-- src:11448 | Order of detention
-- src:11449 | (6) Unless the accused, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows cause why the accused’s detention in custody is not justified by clearly demonstrating that their proposed release plan addresses the risks posed by the accused as they relate to the grounds referred to in subsection (10), the justice shall order, despite any provision of this section, that the accused be detained in custody until the accused is dealt with according to law, if the accused is charged
-- src:11450 | (a) with an indictable offence, other than an offence listed in section 469,
-- src:11451 | (i) that is alleged to have been committed while at large after being released in respect of another indictable offence pursuant to the provisions of this Part or section 679 or 680,
-- src:11452 | (ii) that is an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a serious offence alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization,
-- src:11453 | (iii) that is an offence under any of sections 83.02 to 83.04 and 83.18 to 83.23 or otherwise is alleged to be a terrorism offence,
-- src:11454 | (iv) that is an offence under subsection 16(1) or (2), 17(1), 19(1), 20(1), 20.1(1), 20.3(1), 20.4(1) or 22(1) of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act,
-- src:11455 | (v) that is an offence under subsection 21(1) or section 23 of the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act committed in relation to an offence referred to in subparagraph (iv),
-- src:11456 | (vi) that is an offence under section 95, 98, 98.1, 99, 100, 102 or 103,
-- src:11457 | (vii) that is an offence under section 244 or 244.2, or an offence under section 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 that is alleged to have been committed with a firearm,
-- src:11458 | (viii) that is alleged to involve, or whose subject-matter is alleged to be, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition or prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance, and that is alleged to have been committed while the accused was under a prohibition order within the meaning of subsection 84(1),
-- src:11459 | (ix) that is an offence under any of sections 266 to 268 and 271 to 273 in the commission of which the accused is alleged to have choked, suffocated or strangled the complainant,
-- src:11460 | (x) that is an offence under section 279.01 or 279.011,
-- src:11461 | (xi) that is an offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4),
-- src:11462 | (xii) that is an offence under subsection 346 in the commission of which violence was allegedly used, threatened or attempted against any person,
-- src:11463 | (xii.1) that is an offence in the commission of which violence was allegedly used and that would constitute the accused’s third or subsequent indictable offence in the commission of which violence was used,
-- src:11464 | (xiii) that is an offence under paragraph 348(1)(d), or
-- src:11465 | (xiv) that is an offence under section 117 or 118 of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act;
-- src:11466 | (b) with an indictable offence, other than an offence listed in section 469 and is not ordinarily resident in Canada,
-- src:11467 | (b.1) with an offence in the commission of which violence was allegedly used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner, and the accused
-- src:11468 | (i) has been previously convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any intimate partner of the accused, or
-- src:11469 | (ii) was, at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed, subject to a recognizance entered into under section 810, 810.02, 810.03, 810.1 or 810.2, in the case where the information for the recognizance was laid on behalf of any intimate partner of the accused;
-- src:11470 | (b.2) with an offence in the commission of which violence was allegedly used, threatened or attempted against a person with the use of a weapon, and the accused has been previously convicted, within 10 years of the day on which they were charged for that offence, of another offence in the commission of which violence was also used, threatened or attempted against any person with the use of a weapon, if the maximum term of imprisonment for each of those offences is 10 years or more;
-- src:11471 | (c) with an offence under any of subsections 145(2) to (5) that is alleged to have been committed while they were at large after being released in respect of another offence under the provisions of this Part or section 679, 680 or 816; or
-- src:11472 | (d) with having committed an offence punishable by imprisonment for life under any of sections 5 to 7 of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the offence of conspiring to commit such an offence.
@ref s 515(6) (src:11448-11472)
DECLARE `s 515(6)(a) the charge` HAS
    `the offence charged`                                                                    IS A `s 493.01 the offence charged`
    `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469`                                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is under the Criminal Code`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Code provision the offence is under`                                                IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `(i) the offence is alleged to have been committed while at large after being released in respect of another indictable offence pursuant to the provisions of this Part or section 679 or 680`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2 serious offence: the offence is one`                                                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the offence is alleged to have been committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization`   IS A BOOLEAN
