§ `Section 515(10) -- The grounds on which detention in custody is justified`

-- src:11482 | Justification for detention in custody
-- src:11483 | (10) For the purposes of this section, the detention of an accused in custody is justified only on one or more of the following grounds:
-- src:11484 | (a) where the detention is necessary to ensure his or her attendance in court in order to be dealt with according to law;
-- src:11485 | (b) where the detention is necessary for the protection or safety of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years, having regard to all the circumstances including any substantial likelihood that the accused will, if released from custody, commit a criminal offence or interfere with the administration of justice; and
-- src:11486 | (c) if the detention is necessary to maintain confidence in the administration of justice, having regard to all the circumstances, including
-- src:11487 | (i) the apparent strength of the prosecution’s case,
-- src:11488 | (ii) the gravity of the offence,
-- src:11489 | (iii) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence, including whether a firearm was used,
-- src:11490 | (iv) the fact that the accused is liable, on conviction, for a potentially lengthy term of imprisonment or, in the case of an offence that involves, or whose subject-matter is, a firearm, a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of three years or more, and
-- src:11491 | (v) the number or gravity of any outstanding charges against the accused that arise out of separate events.
@ref s 515(10) (src:11482-11491)
GIVEN `the detention is necessary to ensure the accused's attendance in court in order to be dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the detention is necessary for the protection or safety of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the detention is necessary to maintain confidence in the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(10) the detention of the accused in custody can be justified on one of the three grounds` MEANS
    IF `the detention is necessary to ensure the accused's attendance in court in order to be dealt with according to law`   -- (a)
       OR `the detention is necessary for the protection or safety of the public, including any victim of or witness to the offence, or any person under the age of 18 years`   -- (b)
       OR `the detention is necessary to maintain confidence in the administration of justice`   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the detention of an accused in custody is justified only on one or more of the following grounds"

DECLARE `s 515(10)(c) a circumstance the text names` IS ONE OF
    `s 515(10)(c)(i) the apparent strength of the prosecution's case`
    `s 515(10)(c)(ii) the gravity of the offence`
    `s 515(10)(c)(iii) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence, including whether a firearm was used`
    `s 515(10)(c)(iv) the fact that the accused is liable, on conviction, for a potentially lengthy term of imprisonment or, in the case of an offence that involves, or whose subject-matter is, a firearm, a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of three years or more`
    `s 515(10)(c)(v) the number or gravity of any outstanding charges against the accused that arise out of separate events`
    `s 515(10)(c) a circumstance the text does not name`

@ref s 515(10)(c)(i)-(v) (src:11486-11491)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 515(10)(c) a circumstance the text names`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 515(10)(c) the circumstance is one the text names for the third ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c)(i) the apparent strength of the prosecution's case` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c)(ii) the gravity of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c)(iii) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence, including whether a firearm was used` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c)(iv) the fact that the accused is liable, on conviction, for a potentially lengthy term of imprisonment or, in the case of an offence that involves, or whose subject-matter is, a firearm, a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of three years or more` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c)(v) the number or gravity of any outstanding charges against the accused that arise out of separate events` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 515(10)(c) a circumstance the text does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "having regard to all the circumstances, including"
